'''tollery†''' (tō′lėr-i), ''n.'' [< ME. *''tollerie, tolrie''; < ''toll''<sup>1</sup> + ''-ery''.] The taking of tolls; tax-collecting.

{{smaller block|Petre wente aȝen to fishing, but Mathew not to his ''tolrie.''
